{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "label": "Gold Module \u2014 Architecture & UI/UX Review", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four-part review of app/gold, app/api/gold, lib/gold and the Gold Prisma models with file:line citations for every finding. Chapter 7 catalogues every action item; chapter 13 is the canonical execution order: trust the ledger, trust permissions, trust posting, trust imports, then improve operator experience."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_append_only_violation", "label": "P0-1 \u2014 GoldInventoryEvent is not append-only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, \u00a72 #1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named the single most dangerous finding: import-cleanup and the commit route deleteMany from the ledger on rollback, so any reconciliation snapshot taken before a rollback is silently invalidated with no audit trail. Every other ledger-grade guarantee flows through this table."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_fifo_race", "label": "P0-2 \u2014 FIFO sale linking race", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3 P0-1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "linkFifoSale reads the unsold pool then creates receipts with no lock. The @@unique([goldDispatchId, goldPourId]) does not fire when goldDispatchId is NULL because Postgres treats NULLs as distinct, so two concurrent commits double-sell a pour. Fix is a partial unique index or an advisory lock."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_float_money_columns", "label": "P0-3 \u2014 Float for all weights and money", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #3, \u00a73.3 P1-13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Balances drift over thousands of events and Math.max(0, +(x).toFixed(4)) silently masks negative balances so real oversells become invisible. The +(x).toFixed(N) idiom appears 30+ times papering over Float math; converting to Decimal is named the single biggest correctness improvement."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_multi_tenant_scoping_gap", "label": "P0-4 \u2014 Tenancy reached via site.companyId", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without companyId on the root rows, per-company uniques on pourBarId and receiptNumber are impossible to enforce."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_missing_role_gates", "label": "P0-5 \u2014 No role gates on Gold mutations", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any clerk can commit a 500-row CSV that creates payroll liabilities and journal entries, because pours, purchases, dispatches, receipts, imports, commit and rollback are all ungated."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_ignored_accounting_events", "label": "P0-6 \u2014 dispatch-created and pour-created queued as IGNORED", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, \u00a72 #6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The second most dangerous finding: the GL never debits Gold In-Transit (1300) or Gold Inventory (1250). The integration looks like it works because events appear in the table, but several event types are dead on arrival."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_accounting_outside_tx", "label": "P0-2 \u2014 Accounting captured outside the source transaction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3 P0-2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven endpoints call captureAccountingEvent after the transaction returns, so a process killed in between leaves the source row committed with no journal entries. Fix is a tx parameter on captureAccountingEvent and createJournalEntryFromSource, or a transactional outbox."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_mixed_site_dispatch", "label": "P0-8 \u2014 Cross-site pours in one dispatch", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3 P0-3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dispatch stores one siteId taken from the primary pour, so receipts queried by site misattribute siblings from other sites. Fix is to reject mixed-site dispatches or model M:N with per-site allocation."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_shift_group_scoping", "label": "P0-9 \u2014 Attendance not scoped by shiftGroupId", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3 P0-5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Attendance pulled by (siteId, date, shift) alone dilutes per-worker share when two crews share a shift label, and the matching unique constraint means only one allocation can exist per day+shift+site. Fix scopes by shiftGroupId and widens the unique."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_hydration_hazard", "label": "P0-10 \u2014 toLocaleString hydration hazard on list pages", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #10, \u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The earlier date hotfix only patched import pages, leaving React #418/#310 latent on pours, purchases, dispatches, receipts and allocations lists. Fixed by routing dates through <ClientDate>."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_import_workflow_redesign", "label": "Import workflow redesign (chapter 9)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Import is the strategic surface: mines run paper or Excel ledgers and import is the recurring reconciliation between their books and the system. The 985-line route plus 1182-line page is hot-fixed but not engineered for that mission \u2014 lifecycle states, background worker, mapping presets, period-close, reconciliation reports, append-only rollback and a UI lock for concurrent operators."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_operational_runbook", "label": "Operational runbook for the import workflow (chapter 12)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a712", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Operator daily flow, permissions matrix, incident and investigation playbooks, SLOs/SLIs, escalation matrix and recovery drills \u2014 the source Epic 13 draws its three SLIs, escalation windows and first drill from."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_roadmap_stack_rank", "label": "Roadmap \u2014 Product Planning stack rank (chapter 13)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a713", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The authoritative sequencing for delivery, with a definition-of-done per priority bucket and an explicit 'what not to do yet' list. Chapter 7 says what to fix; chapter 13 says in what order."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_testing_baseline", "label": "Testing baseline and pre-flight gates (chapter 11)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a711", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Test gates that must exist before any P0 migration ships, plus a test pyramid, data factories, CI integration and ownership \u2014 migrations to Decimal and companyId are too risky without witnesses."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_import_studio", "label": "Import Studio \u2014 power-user workbench (Epics 14\u201317)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a716", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Builds on the Epic 9.0 schema additions to give power users a workbench over the import surface, split across four epics with its own done-when criteria."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_goldinventoryevent", "label": "GoldInventoryEvent model", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "prisma/schema.prisma:2296-2317", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Very high volume, critical: the append-style ledger of IN/OUT grams that getOnHandGrams and every balance read depends on."}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_linkfifosale", "label": "linkFifoSale", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "lib/gold/fifo-link.ts:63-138", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_captureaccountingevent", "label": "captureAccountingEvent", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "lib/accounting/integration.ts:75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_architectural_opportunities", "label": "Gold architectural opportunities", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decimal columns, a transactional outbox for accounting, flattening the importer into a job, promoting lifecycle states so voids need not be deletions, M:N multi-site dispatches, corrections as a real table, centralised FIFO locking, one source of truth for the unsold-pour filter, currency on receipts and a consistent capability model."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_append_only_violation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, \u00a72", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_fifo_race", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #2", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_float_money_columns", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #3", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_multi_tenant_scoping_gap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #4", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_missing_role_gates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #5", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_ignored_accounting_events", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #6", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_accounting_outside_tx", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_mixed_site_dispatch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #8", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_shift_group_scoping", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #9", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_hydration_hazard", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/gold-module-review-2026-05-09.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 #10, \u00a710", "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_gold_module_review_2026_05_09_doc", "target": "do